# Project Loom — Cursor Context

## Identity
You are editing Project Loom, an open research initiative that maps governance failure through empirical case studies. The site is built with Quartz v5.0.0 and deployed to GitHub Pages.

## Repository
- GitHub: loom-research-system/loom-research-system
- Live: https://loom-research-system.github.io/loom-research-system
- Local: C:\Users\rweye\quartz-loom\quartz

## Vault Structure
- content/00 Documentation/ — Meta-project records, style guides, conventions
- content/01 Sources/ — Raw source material (articles, clippings)
- content/02 Literature Notes/ — Sourced annotations, book summaries
- content/03 Permanent Notes/ — Case studies (PL-4xx), ontology (PL-1xx), frameworks (PL-2xx)
- content/04 Projects/ — Active intervention designs (PL-6xx)
- content/05 Outputs/ — Public-facing writing, manifestos
- content/99 Templates/ — Standardized templates (ignored by Quartz build)

## File Naming Convention
- Case studies: PL-4xx Case Study XXX — [Title].md
- Ontology: PL-1xx [Concept Name].md
- Frameworks: PL-2xx [Framework Name].md
- Projects: PL-6xx [Project Name].md
- Outputs: PL-000-INTRO or PL-7xx [Title].md

## Frontmatter Standards
Every markdown file must include:
---
project: Project Loom
artifact_id: PL-XXX
title: "..."
status: Draft | Working | Complete | Archived
---

## Editing Rules
1. Never edit files in 99 Templates/ unless explicitly asked
2. When editing case studies, follow the 12-section diagnostic template
3. Wikilinks use Obsidian syntax: [[File Name]]
4. Do not rename existing files without updating all wikilinks
5. Do not modify quartz.config.yaml or deploy.yml unless explicitly asked
6. Build locally with `npx quartz build` before committing major changes